WEBVTT

00:02.480 --> 00:05.450
Ah... the year is already ending.

00:05.450 --> 00:08.050
It got by so fast it's depressing.

00:08.050 --> 00:11.160
The more you grow up, the more the years pass you by.

00:13.630 --> 00:20.530
At this pace, when I'll be an old man, one year will pass as fast as a Formula 1.

00:20.900 --> 00:22.900
I still have time.

00:25.170 --> 00:30.480
No, no, in fact it's already going at the Ben Johnson's speed.

00:25.170 --> 00:30.480
Note: Ben Johnson is a Canadian sprinter native of Jamaica.

00:30.710 --> 00:32.640
He's already here, that Ben.

00:32.640 --> 00:37.220
Don't be so confident because you are young. He'll soon be after you, that Ben.

00:37.220 --> 00:39.720
Seriously? Ben will be coming?

00:39.720 --> 00:42.820
I prefer Carl over Ben. He's cooler.

00:39.720 --> 00:42.820
Note: Carl Lewis was Ben Johnson's rival.

00:44.060 --> 00:48.490
Anyway, this year wasn't that bad in the end.

00:52.130 --> 00:53.200
It's not finished yet!

00:53.200 --> 00:55.330
What do you mean it wasn't that bad in the end?!

00:55.330 --> 00:58.800
Ever since the movie, 6 months went by, and the only job we did was rediffusion!

00:58.800 --> 01:02.470
Well, it's the same recycled sequence like every time...

01:02.940 --> 01:03.580
That's right!

01:03.580 --> 01:06.280
The texts and illustrations have been the same for 4 years.

01:06.880 --> 01:09.110
Do your job more seriously damn it!

01:09.750 --> 01:10.180
Seriously...

01:10.180 --> 01:12.080
It's a special episode you know!

01:12.080 --> 01:16.050
Aniplex-san clearly said he would add exclusive content.

01:16.050 --> 01:18.490
If we start by using recycled content, what will we do?

01:18.490 --> 01:21.430
In fact, this scene was remastered in reality, right?

01:21.430 --> 01:24.060
How long are you gonna pretend that it is that old sequence?

01:24.060 --> 01:27.700
Nowadays it takes more efforts to make it in 4:3.

01:27.700 --> 01:30.140
Alright, alright, I understand.

01:30.140 --> 01:32.140
Then, side panels, open!

01:35.640 --> 01:37.810
But you know Pattsuan,

01:37.810 --> 01:43.320
In fact, that episode, is meant for an important announcement, right?

01:43.320 --> 01:44.650
Don't you think it's kind of embarrassing?

01:44.650 --> 01:45.980
Eh? What is?

01:45.980 --> 01:48.120
Don't act like you don't know...

01:48.120 --> 01:52.520
They talk about an "important announcement", but everybody already knows what it is, don't you think?

01:52.520 --> 01:55.090
Anyway the information has already been revealed in JUMP.

01:55.090 --> 01:57.830
Don't underestimate the enormous internet community.

01:57.830 --> 02:00.070
Hey, don't say such things so lightly!

02:00.070 --> 02:04.270
The content is already revealed, and they insist with their "important announcement"...

02:04.270 --> 02:06.070
How embarrassing....

02:07.670 --> 02:10.280
Wait you two, that's not it!

02:10.280 --> 02:16.150
Even if people have already realized what it is, it doesn't change the fact that it's an important announcement. Let's do it proudly!

02:16.150 --> 02:17.020
Is that so?

02:17.020 --> 02:17.980
Yes it is!

02:18.420 --> 02:21.350
It's a bit embarrassing, but here I go...

02:23.320 --> 02:26.290
The movie Gintama, re-adaptation of the Benizakura Arc!

02:26.290 --> 02:29.330
For the buyers of the DVD collector edition,

02:29.330 --> 02:31.330
here is an important announcement!

02:31.330 --> 02:34.730
IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT

02:37.100 --> 02:38.600
Sorry for the wait!

02:39.170 --> 02:40.340
This time,

02:40.340 --> 02:41.810
for the movie,

02:43.710 --> 02:46.280
the release date for the Blu-Ray has been decided!

02:46.280 --> 02:47.480
What the hell are you saying?!

02:48.150 --> 02:49.450
That's not it, right?

02:49.450 --> 02:53.850
Like we could announce something so disappointing to the people who generously bought the DVD?!

02:53.850 --> 02:57.020
It's not a even a bonus, it's not even worth an official announcement!

02:57.020 --> 02:58.260
W-Well...

02:58.260 --> 03:01.860
The thing the viewers already knew... well...

03:01.860 --> 03:02.960
I thought it was that...

03:02.960 --> 03:06.260
It happens a lot in animes, it's a dirty business.

03:06.260 --> 03:09.670
Shut up! Don't say things that could put us in trouble!

03:09.670 --> 03:17.240
There's no release date yet for the Blu-Ray release (Aniplex)

03:11.670 --> 03:12.070
Look!

03:12.070 --> 03:13.870
Even Aniplex-san says so.

03:13.870 --> 03:16.040
It's written "no release date yet".

03:16.040 --> 03:17.240
Don't mind the details!

03:18.010 --> 03:18.540
Seriously...

03:18.540 --> 03:21.950
An important announcement with that kind of timing, there's only that, right?

03:21.950 --> 03:25.820
The TV series coming back and the start of the second period!

03:30.520 --> 03:32.620
The second period... you say?
- The second period... you say?

03:33.060 --> 03:36.260
So, if we look surprised like that, it's pretty important announcement-like, right?

03:36.260 --> 03:38.430
No... it looks even more forced.

03:38.430 --> 03:40.200
That's right...

03:40.200 --> 03:43.440
Just announcing a second period doesn't fire me up.

03:43.440 --> 03:45.470
It lacks that feeling of importance.

03:45.470 --> 03:48.840
No... just the fact of announcing the restart of the anime is already sufficiently important.

03:48.840 --> 03:50.780
Don't say stupid things.

03:50.780 --> 03:54.310
Even if during that period there was a movie, it's been a year, a year.

03:54.310 --> 03:57.250
The viewers' heart is something that is easily swayed.

03:57.250 --> 04:02.020
During that break time there has been hundreds of new animes created you know,

04:02.020 --> 04:05.760
everybody already forgot about this anime and are going <i>Let's Party</i> or,

04:02.020 --> 04:05.760
Note: <i>Let's Party</i> is Date Masamune's favorite line from <i>Sengoku Basara</i> season 2.

04:05.760 --> 04:08.790
they are busy watching that new thing on the Shinsengumi.

04:05.760 --> 04:08.790
Note: Reference to <i>Hakuouki Shinsengumi Kitan</i>.

04:08.790 --> 04:12.560
Inside all of this, how are we supposed to act when we get back?

04:12.560 --> 04:15.000
"It is with much embarrassment, but I have returned",

04:12.560 --> 04:16.670
Note: Declaration now popular made by Yokoi Shouichi, a Japanese soldier of the 2nd World War who stayed hidden for 28 years.

04:15.000 --> 04:16.670
and doing it in Yokoi-san's style?

04:16.670 --> 04:21.570
Or like Gashu*n or Goto M*ki, is it fine if we come back with some minor changes?

04:16.670 --> 04:21.570
Note: Gashuin Tatsuya is an actor (Densha Otoko, The Taste of Tea). Goto Maki is an ex-idol that completely changes her appearance throughout the years.

04:22.240 --> 04:28.680
To begin with, following the plans of the producers, continuing the anime 6 months after the movie's success wouldn't have been a problem.

04:29.150 --> 04:33.120
Things went slowly because of the consequences of the recession, it's already been a whole year...

04:33.120 --> 04:36.490
The fact of doing a second period augments the risk of declining.

04:36.490 --> 04:39.760
We would need an important announcement with some impact like...

04:39.760 --> 04:41.090
Not like it's that important anyway...

04:41.090 --> 04:43.800
Hey, I did say that this is a bonus episode, right?

04:43.800 --> 04:45.130
You talk too much.

04:45.130 --> 04:46.800
Impact, you say?

04:47.470 --> 04:47.770
Oh!

04:47.770 --> 04:49.940
Why not doing the second period with something like that?

04:49.940 --> 04:52.500
IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT

04:52.500 --> 04:54.770
The anime Gintama, will, this spring

04:54.770 --> 04:57.280
come back with full force!!

04:59.310 --> 05:01.150
Eh, what is this Kagura-chan?

05:01.150 --> 05:02.480
Seems like the picture is blurry.

05:02.480 --> 05:06.180
It's a specialty of the anime Gintama, the fixed plan in 3D!

05:06.180 --> 05:07.850
Eh? That's 3D?

05:07.850 --> 05:09.220
That thing that's really popular right now?

05:09.220 --> 05:13.730
Everybody, buy some red and blue cellos, make glasses out of it and the depth effect is gonna be the best!

05:13.730 --> 05:14.860
Wait a little!

05:14.860 --> 05:19.000
Nowadays red and blue 3D is... isn't it a bit outdated?

05:19.000 --> 05:20.400
Budget problem.

05:20.400 --> 05:24.600
By the way, we finally get to be in 3D, but it's still the same plan as always.

05:24.600 --> 05:27.670
Even if we show this as a free bonus, this won't please anybody, will it?

05:27.670 --> 05:29.140
Budget problem.

05:29.140 --> 05:32.180
Eh!? There was no money to that extent to make this bonus?!

05:32.180 --> 05:34.810
Tsch, you leave me no choice...

05:34.810 --> 05:38.620
If we use some recycled CG, there will be a bit more depth.

05:38.620 --> 05:40.590
Oh, that's me! Impressive!

05:40.590 --> 05:42.490
With this we get a little the feeling of depth!

05:42.490 --> 05:46.930
Then since we're in 3D, we need projections, right?

05:46.930 --> 05:48.590
Eh? There's still something more?

05:48.590 --> 05:49.260
Here you go!

05:51.300 --> 05:54.170
So that's how it is, please make the second period be in 3D.

05:54.170 --> 05:55.370
No way it's gonna happen!

05:55.370 --> 05:57.070
Why is that?

05:57.070 --> 06:00.310
With this it's become an announcement with enough impact.

06:00.310 --> 06:03.070
How is it necessary to make it in 3D?

06:03.070 --> 06:05.910
Don't be deceived by the impact and don't make false announcements!

06:05.910 --> 06:08.950
Then, since we're between us and talking of important announcements,

06:08.950 --> 06:10.920
starting from the second period, the voice actors will change,

06:10.920 --> 06:13.720
it's been decided that they will all be good-looking celebrities.

06:13.720 --> 06:14.390
Hey, wait.

06:14.390 --> 06:16.620
I want my voice to be done by  Mizushima H*iro!

06:14.390 --> 06:16.620
Note: Mizushima Hiro is an actor (Kamen Rider Kabuto, Lovely Complex) and a voice actor (The Incredible Hulk).

06:16.860 --> 06:18.960
Then my voice will be Ay*ka!

06:16.860 --> 06:18.960
Note: Ayaka is a singer and Mizushima Hiro's spouse since 2009.

06:18.960 --> 06:20.590
That has a lot of impact!
- Listen to me you two!

06:21.030 --> 06:23.830
Then there is the staff direction.

06:23.830 --> 06:25.030
We'd need P*xar...

06:25.030 --> 06:25.460
Hey!

06:25.460 --> 06:26.830
No, here we definitely need Ghi*li.

06:25.460 --> 06:28.770
Note: Studio Ghibli was founded by Miyazaki Hayao and Takahata Isao, they produced <i>Laputa, Totoro, Princess Mononoke, etc...</i>

06:26.830 --> 06:28.770
The author seems to like them too.

06:28.770 --> 06:31.040
Stop your nonsense!

06:36.240 --> 06:37.710
It's alright already you two!

06:37.710 --> 06:40.110
It was my bad to focus on that thing's importance!

06:40.110 --> 06:43.110
Anyway the announcement's content has already been revealed, so we do as always!

06:43.110 --> 06:43.950
Ehhhhhh?
- Ehhhhhh?

06:43.950 --> 06:45.150
Give up!

06:45.750 --> 06:47.120
Now, like this!

06:47.120 --> 06:49.720
IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT

06:49.720 --> 06:52.020
The anime Gintama

06:52.020 --> 06:54.530
TV series comes back!!

06:54.530 --> 06:55.690
ANPAN

06:54.530 --> 07:00.770
Note: Anpan is a japanese sweet made with anko, a sweet red bean paste.

06:55.690 --> 06:57.230
Anpan mode of life: 4th day...

06:58.100 --> 06:59.560
Anpan mode of life: 12th day...

06:59.560 --> 07:00.770
Anpan mode of life: 15th day...

07:00.770 --> 07:01.700
Anpan mode of life: 20th day...

07:01.700 --> 07:02.400
Anpan mode of life: 21st day...

07:02.400 --> 07:03.000
Anpan mode of life: 22nd day...

07:03.000 --> 07:03.570
Anpan mode of life: 23rd day...

07:03.570 --> 07:04.140
Anpan mode of life: 24th day...

07:04.140 --> 07:05.100
Anpan mode of life: 25th day...

07:05.100 --> 07:06.300
Anpan mode of life: 28th day...

07:06.300 --> 07:08.040
Anpan mode of life: 30th day...

07:08.040 --> 07:09.210
WISH CARDS

07:09.210 --> 07:11.140
Are they stupid or what?

07:11.140 --> 07:12.540
Every last one of them,

07:11.140 --> 07:13.550
This year,
Taiga was
about
Ryouma,
right?

07:11.140 --> 07:14.980
Note: Each year, NHK releases a "Taiga": an historical drama running all year round. The 2009 edition was about Sakamoto Ryouma, an important japanese historical figure which inspired Sakamoto Tatsuma in Gintama.

07:12.540 --> 07:14.980
why do they put so much energy in writing those cards?

07:13.550 --> 07:14.650
WE GOT MARRIED

07:13.550 --> 07:14.650
Best wishes
on our behalf.

07:13.550 --> 07:14.650
Sakata Gintoki
& Ayame
(maiden name: Sarutobi)

07:13.550 --> 07:14.650
Otae,
I'm
sorry,
I got
ahead.

07:15.280 --> 07:17.120
This world is lead by the Sazae-san law,

07:15.280 --> 07:19.180
Note: Sazae-san makes reference to the anime of the same name that's been on since 1969 with the characters never aging.

07:17.520 --> 07:19.180
the years don't renew for ever!

07:19.550 --> 07:20.690
VALENTINE'S DAY

07:20.690 --> 07:23.690
Why don't you give some to Gin-san and the others once in a while?

07:23.690 --> 07:25.660
Ehh? No way!

07:25.660 --> 07:27.090
I don't like them...

07:27.090 --> 07:28.460
Those idiots.

07:28.890 --> 07:29.460
Oh?

07:29.460 --> 07:30.500
KANDAN MUSUME

07:29.460 --> 07:32.330
Note: A kandan musume is a "star seller" that brings clients to a business.

07:30.230 --> 07:30.800
Old hag!

07:31.260 --> 07:32.460
Remember this!

07:32.460 --> 07:34.470
I'll definitely make a formidable shop

07:34.470 --> 07:36.430
better than your rundown place!

07:36.430 --> 07:38.540
I'll definitely become

07:38.540 --> 07:40.540
a lot more of a "big" woman than you!

07:41.140 --> 07:42.170
DATE

07:42.170 --> 07:43.270
Kondo-san,

07:43.270 --> 07:45.410
There's no mistake that this is a trap...

07:45.410 --> 07:48.980
Being of the same sadistic nature, I understand perfectly what he's thinking...

07:48.980 --> 07:51.250
No matter if it rains water or lances,

07:51.250 --> 07:53.750
my rain of love will never stop!

07:53.750 --> 07:54.650
MONKEY

07:55.690 --> 07:57.060
Putting aside his aggressivity,

07:57.490 --> 07:59.020
he at least learned to reflect on his actions.

07:59.690 --> 08:01.060
There's only one problem...

08:02.130 --> 08:03.460
In fact this monkey...

08:04.260 --> 08:05.830
still has no name.

08:05.830 --> 08:06.930
POOL

08:06.930 --> 08:10.670
I asked you to be ready to watch the clients to prevent them from drowning!

08:10.670 --> 08:12.740
I finally found a job.

08:12.740 --> 08:13.570
I beg you!

08:13.570 --> 08:15.340
Act more seriously!

08:15.740 --> 08:16.840
GLASSES

08:16.840 --> 08:17.940
I...

08:17.940 --> 08:20.350
I'll think of these glasses as Gin-san

08:20.350 --> 08:22.080
and won't leave them for a minute.

08:22.080 --> 08:25.020
I'll always... treasure them!

08:25.020 --> 08:26.180
ULTIMATE TECHNIQUE

08:26.180 --> 08:27.650
Look, Gintoki!

08:27.650 --> 08:31.320
While you were slacking during the anime break,

08:31.320 --> 08:34.830
I trained to develop my Ultimate Technique!

08:34.830 --> 08:36.330
FUNERALS

08:36.330 --> 08:39.530
He's back from the depths of hell...

08:39.530 --> 08:42.300
These funerals are bad...

08:42.300 --> 08:43.540
If I do something wrong...

08:43.540 --> 08:45.700
the old man will curse me to death!

08:45.700 --> 08:46.970
VILLAINS

08:46.970 --> 08:50.180
I wonder if it's about time to show my gratitude...

08:50.180 --> 08:51.940
to that samurai...

08:53.210 --> 08:54.680
That idiot...

08:54.680 --> 08:57.350
I will kill him in your stead...

08:57.350 --> 09:00.350
And then, war arises in the Kabuki District

09:00.350 --> 09:01.650
What?

09:01.650 --> 09:04.220
The strongest man in the Kabuki District?

09:04.720 --> 09:07.090
You're new around these parts, right?

09:07.090 --> 09:08.730
There are some from time to time...

09:08.730 --> 09:13.330
that come here thinking they can make a name for themselves, these foolish punks...

09:15.430 --> 09:18.440
First there are four unbelievable monsters.

09:19.100 --> 09:21.470
The fierce god, Mademoiselle Saigou.

09:21.470 --> 09:24.780
The powerful Doromizu Jirochou.

09:24.780 --> 09:26.380
The Princess Paon Kada.

09:26.380 --> 09:28.580
The Impress, Otose.

09:28.580 --> 09:32.920
These four are feared as the "Four Celestial Emperors"

09:31.400 --> 09:35.250
FOUR
CELESTIAL
EMPERORS
ARC

09:31.400 --> 09:35.250
KABUKI
DISTRICT'S

09:32.920 --> 09:35.250
in all the Kabuki District.

09:36.520 --> 09:37.420
Eeeehhh?

09:37.420 --> 09:38.560
An assassin?

09:38.560 --> 09:40.530
This idiot?

09:40.530 --> 09:44.100
A girl this stupid would be the yakuza's cannon fodder?

09:44.100 --> 09:47.870
There's no need for us to oppose each other...

09:47.870 --> 09:49.970
Our enemy...

09:50.670 --> 09:52.870
is none other than Jirochou, isn't it?

09:54.310 --> 09:56.410
Those who are prepared to get their balls ripped off...

09:56.410 --> 09:59.540
I hope you are ready, you bastards!

10:00.040 --> 10:01.610
Me? Having influence?

10:01.610 --> 10:03.550
I never had any...

10:04.380 --> 10:05.550
They are...

10:05.550 --> 10:07.090
no use at all.

10:05.550 --> 10:07.090
I am fed up to wait for your rent.

10:05.550 --> 10:07.090
Take your idiots with you and

10:05.550 --> 10:07.090
hurry up and leave.

10:05.550 --> 10:07.090
Don't ever come back to this town.

10:05.550 --> 10:07.090
Otose

10:08.220 --> 10:08.690
They are only...

10:09.750 --> 10:11.260
my family you see...

10:11.820 --> 10:16.030
Old haaaaggggg!

10:19.860 --> 10:23.000
Broadcast starts in April 2011

10:23.840 --> 10:25.640
How was it? With this style?

10:25.640 --> 10:27.840
Well, it was normal...

10:27.840 --> 10:30.280
It would have been better made by Ghi*li after all.

10:30.280 --> 10:31.340
You're persistent!

10:33.340 --> 10:38.480
On that note, to you who bought the movie's DVD, it's already the time for us to leave.

10:38.480 --> 10:42.950
Then, we will see you again for the second period of the anime Gintama.

10:42.950 --> 10:44.990
With us the Yorozuya,

10:44.990 --> 10:46.560
let's meet again!

10:49.660 --> 10:52.600
But still, Sadaharu really won't wake up...
